From: =?UTF-8?q?Darrel=20Gri=C3=ABt?= <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 15:41:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] v10: Report minnow's real 45Hz vsync period
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

minnow's HWC_VSYNC_PERIOD query always fails, so refreshRate() fell
back to 60 Hz. The panel really refreshes at 45 Hz (pixel clock
4176 kHz / 320x290).

Qt's fixed-step animation driver therefore advanced animations 16.7 ms
per frame while frames arrive every 22.2 ms. Flings played at ~75%
speed and hitched whenever the driver drift-corrected to wall time.
The wrong rate also reached every Wayland client through wl_output.

Report the true period instead.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [minnow-specific panel timing]
Signed-off-by: Darrel Griët <dgriet@gmail.com>
---
 hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp
@@ -317,8 +317,8 @@

         int res = hwc_device->query(hwc_device, HWC_VSYNC_PERIOD, &vsyncVal);
         if (res != 0 || vsyncVal == 0) {
-            qWarning() << "query(HWC_VSYNC_PERIOD) failed, assuming 60 Hz";
-            vsyncVal = 16666667; // 60 Hz vsync period in ns
+            qWarning() << "query(HWC_VSYNC_PERIOD) failed, assuming 45 Hz";
+            vsyncVal = 22222222; // minnow panel: 4176 kHz / (320*290) = 45 Hz
         }

         vsyncFPS = (float)1000000000 / (float)vsyncVal;
